// Title: Windows Defender Exclusion List Modified
// Sigma ID: 46a68649-f218-4f86-aea1-16a759d81820
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @BarryShooshooga
// Date: 2019-10-26 | Modified: 2023-11-11
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects modifications to the Windows Defender exclusion registry key. This could indicate a
//   potentially suspicious or even malicious activity by an attacker trying to add a new exclusion
//   in order to bypass security.
// False positives:
//   - Intended exclusions by administrators
// References:
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/gootkit-malware-bypasses-windows-defender-by-setting-path-exclusions/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/builtin/security/win_security_windows_defender_exclusions_registry_modified.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions.*$"
